WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.690
Class 3-B?

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:04.820
Kuroi-sensei!

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:05.900
Yeah, yeah...

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:39.890
Guess what?

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:40.720
My glasses...

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.810
Where are my glasses?

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:42.470
But I've been playing the same fighting games lately.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:43.850
If I don't have my glasses...

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:44.060
But I've been playing the same fighting games lately.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:35.420
Good morning, Kagami.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.300
Yo.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.250
You're in a good mood.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:37.860
What happened?

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:41.530
I trade my old cell phone for a new one.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:42.030
Finally, huh?

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:42.680
Seriously?

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:43.090
Then you can use songs for ringtones and set screensavers.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:44.510
You're actually like a kid.

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:45.640
Wait a sec.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.010
Do you watch anime and stuff then?

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:47.560
Then you can use songs for ringtones and set screensavers.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.790
I already switched to one of my favorites.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:54.210
Mi-Mi-Miracle! Mikurun-run! Mi-Mi-Miracle! Mikurun-run!

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.170
That's some song.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:56.800
But you know...

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:56.820
Mi-Mi-Miracle! Mikurun-run! Mi-Mi-Miracle! Mikurun-run!

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.920
You have to pick up before it gets to the chorus...

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.720
...which makes you stress out and regret it, right?

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.370
And if you don't pick up, they'll hang up anyway.

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.280
I don't really care about that stuff...

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:07.230
Is that how it is?

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.960
If I had to choose, I'd say Kagami's...

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:13.480
...an orc!

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.350
Why?!

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:15.750
I'm the only one who's a monster?!

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.460
Yes, hello?

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:20.780
This is Hiiragi.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.150
Yeah...

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.800
Too used to answering the phone at home.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.240
She was all mad at me a second ago...

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.560
I got a sandwich with balsamic vinegar sauce today...

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.960
How come women can switch moods so quickly?

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.790
But the other day, my mother...

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.810
I'm home!

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:36.460
Yes?

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.500
Hello?

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:38.750
Miyuki?

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:39.820
Geez!

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:40.650
Miyuki!

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:41.820
Here, phone!

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:42.800
From Konata-chan!

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:44.180
Um...

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.070
Did I do something wrong?

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:46.820
No.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.830
My mother is really bad at deception...

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:51.180
...so you can tell when she's mad.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.520
I believe she just hit her leg against the table.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.960
But that wasn't exactly an issue of deception...

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.780
She's exactly the way she seems.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.680
It's a good thing Miyuki knows so much.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.490
I can ask you about anything I don't know.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.450
I enjoyed being praised by Mother...

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.270
...so I became accustomed to looking things up.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.890
<i>Miyuki knows more than Mama does.</i>

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.250
Now, I enjoy learning as well.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.750
So in other words...

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.210
...I did a wonderful job of raising you, right?

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:23.990
That's how the conversation went.

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.300
That's some silly conversation.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:31.830
In any case, I now know that you're
undeniably your mother's daughter.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:32.650
Are we similar?

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.640
Down to the very last gene.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:35.190
But...

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.250
Miyuki isn't just good at studying...

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.150
She knows a lot about all kinds of stuff.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.860
There are many sources of information these days...

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.860
...and it's fun to learn a lot.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.340
I couldn't do it.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:48.930
No motivation!

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:49.930
Wanna play!

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:51.790
Rely on others in a pinch!

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.960
They say that only children and oldest children tend to be selfish...

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:57.500
That's right.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.040
Aren't you an only child?

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.420
I guess it depends on the person.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:03.260
Not at all.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.260
You could say that I had a model...

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.610
...or someone who was like an oldest child...

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:09.470
...in my life.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.140
<i>I don't feel like cleaning!</i>

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.540
<i>Laundry is tiring!</i>

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:13.890
<i>Can we order out?</i>

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.410
In our family...

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.250
...we have two older sisters...

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.330
...and meals turn into battles...

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:20.980
...which helps build character.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:21.520
Yay!

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.800
Sukiyaki!

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.730
Eat up.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.940
Let's eat!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:33.850
And then, Kona-chan...

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:35.100
Oof.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:35.270
And then, Kona-chan...

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:36.330
...said that cell phones go out of service because
of a thick concentration of these something particles.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.850
Mine.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:39.350
...said that cell phones go out of service because
of a thick concentration of these something particles.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:40.670
Really...

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.090
And when her battery runs out...

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:44.650
...she says her phone's out of commission.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:45.380
This one.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:45.400
...she says her phone's out of commission.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:49.530
Modern girls use some strange words.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:50.470
Hey.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.390
Leave enough for Tsukasa.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.720
Tsukasa.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:56.140
You can have mine.

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.140
Thanks.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:58.230
You sound nice...

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.270
...but weren't you stuffing yourself?

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:03.590
So having a lot of siblings can be good and bad.

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:06.200
You can say that about being an only child as well.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.360
That's right.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.740
Yuki-chan, sometimes you really space out, right?

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.470
Space out, is it?

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:12.010
You know...

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:12.830
Like the other day...

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:17.540
I can never get sick of the name elegant sea urchin.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.270
What happened?

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:23.860
I was walking and thinking...

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.030
...and I ended up running into the door.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:28.630
You have incredible concentration, Miyuki-san.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:30.110
That happens a lot, huh?

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.050
Not often, though it's embarrassing.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.030
Huh?

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:36.850
Doesn't it mean you have no
concentration if you start thinking about something...

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.810
...while you're doing something else?

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:39.460
Huh?

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:40.140
Which way is it?

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:42.520
That sounds like something Miyuki would do.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:43.520
Indeed.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.530
The other day, I was warming a drink...

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.400
I forgot.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:52.660
I'll have to reheat it.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.030
One more time...

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.580
And again...

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.540
Geez, Miyuki...

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:03.960
You forgot again, didn't you?

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.610
Sorry, it just happens.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:06.980
You're so hopeless.

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:09.210
I'll bring it to you.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.720
Thank you so much.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.470
Click.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:20.850
I forgot.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.170
Like mother, like daughter.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.730
Though it's embarrassing.

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:28.050
When did you start wearing glasses, Miyuki-san?

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:32.550
Midway through grade school, I believe.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:35.930
So you weren't born nearsighted.

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:37.120
When I was little...

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.080
...I loved how my mother would read to me before I went to sleep....

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.580
...but my mother would fall asleep first...

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:45.170
...and I would want to know what happened...

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.360
...so I would read by myself in the dark room...

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:48.730
...and eventually, my eyes...

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:53.740
But it's best when you're close with your parents like that.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:56.490
The reason kids these days tend to be cold and apathetic...

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:58.030
...may be a lack of...

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:00.680
...parental love or intimacy.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:01.850
That's right...

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:06.150
I wonder when the last time okaa-san gave me a big hug was.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.110
You're clingy...

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:11.650
...so you were really close to her until middle school.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:12.690
Really?

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:14.830
That might be why you're such a good girl.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:19.030
My otou-san is still clingy about me.

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:22.000
That might be why you haven't grown up, in a manner of speaking.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:23.790
Speaking of kids...

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:27.090
...there sure have been a lot cases of kidnapping and confinement.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:30.020
You seem to be sensitive to that stuff.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:32.740
Well, first, I'm worried about my otou-san.

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:34.510
Don't just blurt out scary things.

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:39.330
Well, it more or less has to do with the games I play.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:42.350
I wish they'd stop since it creates problems for other users.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.350
At the very least...

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:46.940
...this stuff doesn't happen in the games I play.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:48.400
Oh, yeah.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.500
It's almost been a year.

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:51.170
Since what?

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.280
Since I started working.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:54.690
My coworkers...

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:56.700
...said they're going to do something to celebrate.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:57.910
That's right.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.160
We've never gone before.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.950
Maybe we'll check out the place you work some time.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.330
As payback for New Year's.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:04.310
Sure.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:05.210
It's okay?!

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.130
Don't people usually hate that?

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.460
Well, half my job is to let other people look at me.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:12.940
It's called a cosplay café, right?

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.490
Let me know before you come.

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:17.530
It can be pretty crowded at times.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:18.660
We'll do that.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:19.740
Hey, you guys.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.620
Class started.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.160
Hello?

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.540
We just left the station.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:32.550
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.030
We'll buy it for you.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.710
Okay. Okay!

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:37.970
Did Kona-chan say it was okay?

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:39.510
It's okay...

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:41.410
...but she wants us to go over there and buy this month's Comp...

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.640
...and the Lelou** comic for her.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.980
I wonder if we can find it quickly.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:50.130
She said to remember to ask the clerk to stamp the receipt...

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.460
Sounds complicated.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:55.780
Excuse me.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:56.340
Do you have a minute?

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.180
Can I take a picture?

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.870
I'm not Kamigishi.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.600
I'm Hiiragi.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.360
Hey!

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:10.850
What are you doing?!

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.810
Could I also get a picture?

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:14.270
Sheesh!

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:15.070
Stop that!

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.200
Excuse me then.

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:18.590
Could you say Hiroyuki-chan?

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:20.760
Hi-Hiroyuki...

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:20.870
...-chan?

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:21.870
We're leaving.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.970
This is the first time I've been in one of these places.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:29.690
It's so big that I'm quite nervous.

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:32.880
She said on the phone that we'd see it once we got there.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.730
Kona-chan would know.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:37.180
I'd get lost if I were alone.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:43.700
Is this it?

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.310
Now we just need the Lelou** comic.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.330
Not here.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:52.570
I can't find it.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:54.190
Excuse me.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.820
Where would I find the Lelou** comic?

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.450
That would be this.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:01.200
Code Ge**s.

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:05.370
You could at least have told us the title...

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:08.660
Can I put this on a point card next time?

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:11.460
Then you'll have to bring this receipt with you.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:12.210
Okay.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.940
Thank you very much!

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:17.090
Now we just have to go find Konata.

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.280
I'm hungry, onee-chan!

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:20.920
I'm almost done working.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:22.100
Hold on a bit.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.910
How are we supposed to find our way?

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:31.160
I looked it up just in case.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:33.620
I believe it's this way.

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:34.880
That's our Yuki-chan!

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:37.070
Guess we can only count on Miyuki.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:38.880
This is the place, right?

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:39.550
Yes.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.280
On the third floor.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:48.470
Welcome back, Master!

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:52.330
You can have a seat here.

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.520
The first hour is 800 yen.

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:59.530
All the soda you can drink.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:01.610
All the games you can play for free.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:03.320
All the sweets you can eat.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:07.850
Can I get this broiled eel?

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:08.640
Currently not available.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:10.870
Then the shrimp pilaf...

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:11.890
Currently impossible.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.440
Then spaghetti with meat sauce.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.310
It will take fifteen minutes.

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:19.110
Permission?

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:20.250
Okay.

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:20.820
Do it.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:23.400
They can do business like that?

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:24.200
You people.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:26.390
What do you want to drink?

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:27.750
H-Hold on a sec!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.200
Hurry it up.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.040
There's a penalty if you take too long! A penalty!

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.790
Is this how you should treat a customer?

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.660
It's how we do things here.

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:35.750
You're done deciding, right?

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.560
I'll have a melon soda.

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:40.010
I have no interest in an ordinary menu.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:42.760
I'll have milk tea.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:44.450
What do you want?

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.030
I'm looking!

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:48.010
A brigade member shouldn't be this slow!

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:49.060
When did I become a brigade member?

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:50.850
That's the setting in this place.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:53.390
You're a hundred years too early to be defying the chief.

00:11:53.390 --> 00:11:55.140
What a pain...

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:56.980
Then give me an ice coffee.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:58.130
Order from the chief!

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.110
Wait here!

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:00.980
Oh, boy...

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.380
Hasn't stunk in a while...

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.330
We're going on stage now, so watch.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:23.480
If we can solve all the mysteries on this planet...

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:27.150
...we can all go anywhere we want!

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:28.660
Even to the end of time!

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:29.620
Boooon!!

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:38.400
Encore! Encore!

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.710
Amazing!

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:41.530
They're all very talented.

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:47.340
Ponytail version next!

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:48.450
Ponytail version, please!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:52.220
She's an exchange student.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:54.580
A first-year at our school.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:58.000
My name is Patricia Martin.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.090
Nice to meet you.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:01.810
We've even put out a CD.

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:03.170
Here.

00:13:03.570 --> 00:13:05.920
Should you really release something like that?

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:07.510
Excuse me.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:08.930
Could I get some tea?

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:11.030
Do you want warm tea?

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:11.620
Yes.

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:13.100
Hot tea please.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:15.290
I'd like a melon soda, please.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.150
Got it.

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:17.350
Uh...

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:19.940
What's this Up-To-Us Mixed Juicy Juice like?

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:21.730
Classified information.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.130
House rules!

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:27.280
This café really exhausts me.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:34.160
M-My height...

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:34.960
Don't worry.

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:38.000
I'm sure you'll grow in time.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.960
Th-That's right.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:42.830
Onee-chan!

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:44.260
Yu-chan.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:48.380
<i>And here's a person to crush my hopes...</i>

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:53.980
H-How much taller have you grown since you entered high school?

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:54.930
Man...

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.450
I haven't grown in either direction.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:59.960
You'd better prepare yourself.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:05.420
No need to fret.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:06.740
You're still in demand.

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:08.550
Hey, you two.

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:10.630
Have you ever been to a class reunion?

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.010
Not yet.

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:14.510
Me neither.

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:15.750
But where did that come from?

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:21.500
Isn't the phrase "you haven't
changed" usually supposed to be a compliment?

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:26.090
But the only people who want to hear
that have probably changed considerably...

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:27.270
...in various places...

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:29.220
So it does concern you.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:30.510
Okay!

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:33.180
Golden Week's starting...

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:33.720
...but listen up.

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:36.350
You've also got tests right after break...

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:38.470
...but don't forget that you're preparing for exams...

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:40.810
...and use your vacation wisely.

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:42.480
Also...

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.860
...you still have a few days left of school before break.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.070
I won't let you take any sick days.

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:47.990
Kamchatka!

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:52.550
<i>The aura emitting from her whole body...</i>

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.550
<i>No question about it.</i>

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:56.200
<i>She's Legendary Girl A.</i>

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.740
<i>Is today's target that new book?</i>

00:14:58.740 --> 00:14:59.660
<i>Or is she after some goods?</i>

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:00.710
<i>Use your head!</i>

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:05.710
<i>Don't forget that we're having a spring audio/visual special!</i>

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:09.880
<i>Not yet!</i>

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.050
<i>Give her enough room.</i>

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:13.110
<i>Recommend an item once she's let her guard down.</i>

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.280
<i>That's right!</i>

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.680
<i>Slowly wait to approach her.</i>

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:19.470
<i>That's it!</i>

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:26.630
<i>Now!</i>

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:27.490
<i>Approach her!</i>

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:28.690
Heading out!

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.920
Welcome!

00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:33.030
We have these new releases!

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:36.260
Kagami?

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:37.330
You made it?

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:39.490
Be right there.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:42.290
Just killing time while waiting for someone?!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.100
When you're boiling something...

00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:47.480
...you use rough cutting...

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:49.670
...and cut them into random shapes.

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:50.320
My...

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:51.630
Really...

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:53.610
That increases the total surface area...

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:55.550
...and lets the taste soak in.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:56.820
Once you've scooped out the Iye...

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:59.530
...you let it cook on medium for around ten minutes.

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:01.240
It'll become soggy if it sits too long...

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:03.500
...so take it out once you can poke through.

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:04.480
I see.

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:06.460
Somehow, when it's home economics...

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:09.590
...Miyuki starts looking below average.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:13.490
Now I know how you see us.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:14.970
Hiiragi-chan.

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:18.800
Want to study for the test together in the library?

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:19.870
Sounds good.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:23.430
Club activities are on hiatus right before a test...

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:24.980
...so there's nothing to do.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:26.920
That's why you study.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.250
That's the point.

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:29.190
Well...

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:31.290
I know that...

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.570
But when my club time is suddenly free...

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:36.260
...it's like a whole new world is open to me.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:40.620
When you look at it that way, I can't waste the time on studying.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:42.280
It gets me all excited.

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:47.960
Anyway, you should realize you're
half the reason for this study session.

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:48.710
Pooped!

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:49.420
That was fast!

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:51.150
Let's take a break!

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:55.030
Maybe you can't concentrate because you have no goal?

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:56.900
Don't you have any dreams for the future?

00:16:56.900 --> 00:16:58.410
Dreams?

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.830
Not really for the future...

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.950
But this time of year, don't you wish you could win the lottery...

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:07.850
...and live the simple life?

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:08.770
Everything's a drag.

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:09.690
Minegishi.

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:11.210
Do something about her.

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:12.960
When I use my head...

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:15.090
...I need sweet stuff!

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:18.340
Once we're done, I'll give you some cookies I baked last time.

00:17:18.340 --> 00:17:19.260
Hang in there.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.660
So you bake sweets and stuff.

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:23.700
Can't compare with that Ajiyoshi boy.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:25.930
Nah, you've got that Ajiyoshi boy licked.

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:28.140
<i>Studying's a pain!</i>

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:29.100
<i>Onee-chan.</i>

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:31.030
<i>I tried making a madeleine.</i>

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:32.810
What's wrong?

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:34.460
Oh, yeah...

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:36.570
I wouldn't lump you with them...

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:40.530
...but I was just thinking that you tend to make similar friends.

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:43.370
Haven't you been overly relaxed...

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:45.470
...because you thought it was only stomatitis?

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:48.770
There sure are a lot more medical programs like this these days.

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:49.770
That's true.

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:52.540
It's scary since it could really happen.

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:53.800
Especially for me.

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:56.960
Actually, after watching this...

00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:00.220
...I start feeling like my time's almost come.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.110
Too many possible causes.

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:05.280
Please stop the depressing talk.

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:05.990
I beg you!

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:06.990
Live!

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:13.960
Onee-chan!

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:15.090
Teach me this part.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.070
Um...

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:21.990
Curses, like chickens, come home to roost?

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:23.620
This means...

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.830
...that Kazu likes chicken.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:28.750
When you go home, you'll find roast chicken...

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.170
...I think?

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:31.440
Nee-san.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:33.060
Translate the next part.

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:35.420
Let's see.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:38.420
When you make the contract...

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:41.110
Did we ever learn this?

00:18:41.110 --> 00:18:42.220
That's right.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.180
This one time when I was working as a shrine maiden...

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:47.640
...a foreigner told me about why the gate is called a torii.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:49.410
What'd he say?

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:52.620
In the past, people believed that birds would carry the dead...

00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:56.730
...so they named it <i>tori</i> (bird) <i>i</i> (here)
because it was a place for birds to rest.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:59.550
They know way more about Japan than we do.

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:02.910
<i>It might have been faster to ask Kagami onee-chan...</i>

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:11.120
The freezing Sea of Japan...

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:13.750
Where have my loved ones gone?

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:17.710
Now she swims solo through the
raging waters of the entertainment industry.

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:19.210
Here's a song.

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:22.150
Kogami Akira with "Cape of Thirty Years."

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:22.900
Hey!

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:24.590
How is this a concert?

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:25.850
This is the best we could do on our budget!

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.550
Don't think you'll get away with this!

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:28.100
It's starting!

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.580
Who do you think I...

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:38.380
Would you mind if I talked to myself?

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:49.760
I softly whispered to the seagulls.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:55.850
Woman, led by a sincere heart...

00:19:56.920 --> 00:20:01.360
Frozen by the northern sea winds...

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:03.900
Gone astray...

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:05.620
Love falls apart...

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:06.740
Drinks are taking a while.

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:10.000
Resentment crumbles...

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:10.680
Yes.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:11.480
Resentment crumbles...

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:13.350
I've brought your drinks.

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:14.630
Unable to reach you so far away...

00:20:14.630 --> 00:20:15.520
Thanks.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.670
Unable to reach you so far away...

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:20.420
I stand still...

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:21.170
Soaked in...

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:21.900
W-W-Wait!

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.170
The brown one's mine!

00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:28.800
Cape of Thirty Years!

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:36.140
Good stuff!

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:43.800
We break down in tears in our own little lodge...

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:44.740
Let's see...

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:48.510
"Exhausting Life Returns" is...

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:49.780
We break down in tears in our own little lodge...

00:20:51.350 --> 00:21:00.840
Regretting that night of love...

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:07.090
Men, making selfish promises...

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:12.220
Never keeping a single one...

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:13.120
Yes?
Thrown right into...

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:13.810
Thrown right into...

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:14.890
That's right.

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:16.000
Extension...

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.640
Thrown right into...

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:17.920
...the spray of the waves...

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.000
It's okay.

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.280
...the spray of the waves...

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:22.010
Yes. Thanks.

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:22.980
...the spray of the waves...

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:24.090
Five minutes left.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:25.050
Unable to meet you so far away...

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:27.720
Time to clean up, clean up.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:28.700
Bye-nee!
Unable to meet you so far away...

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:31.870
I wish to offer you my yearning...
Bye-nee!

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:32.850
Man...

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:35.080
I want to release a song by myself, too.
I wish to offer you my yearning...

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:36.500
Soul of Thirty Years!
I want to release a song by myself, too.

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:39.350
For-For-For-Forgot my something...

00:23:10.820 --> 00:23:13.950
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:14.680
Gloomy!

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:15.530
Nagato.

00:23:15.530 --> 00:23:17.580
Nobody's gonna watch if you're like that.

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:19.560
Sound more like somebody...

00:23:19.560 --> 00:23:23.250
...happily moving from the TV to the
tearoom at 6:30 on a Sunday night.

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:24.380
One more time.

00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:24.750
Go!

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:27.800
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:29.360
Nothing changed!

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:30.710
Forget it.

00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:31.280
Next time:

00:23:31.280 --> 00:23:32.860
Under the Sun.

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:33.900
Look forward to it.

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:35.820
Er, no.

00:23:35.820 --> 00:23:37.160
Rock, paper, scissors!
